WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.358
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.358 --> 00:00:04.441
- [Narrator] Wilbur Force, my friend.

00:00:05.291 --> 00:00:08.291
You used to be The King in the Ring.

00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:11.150
You wrestled for glory.

00:00:12.558 --> 00:00:15.110
You punished your opponents.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.777
You stayed in shape.

00:00:19.704 --> 00:00:20.871
What happened?

00:00:22.258 --> 00:00:24.295
- [William] We just weren't
doing many shows anymore.

00:00:24.295 --> 00:00:27.128
You kind of lose a bit of hope, I guess.

00:00:27.128 --> 00:00:27.961
And I did.

00:00:29.944 --> 00:00:32.152
I miss the physicality of a match,

00:00:32.152 --> 00:00:34.430
I miss cheating and getting away with it,

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.180
and I definitely miss my friends.

00:00:39.428 --> 00:00:41.109
- If someone asks you
why you're into wrestling

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:42.851
and saying that it's all
fake, what would you say?

00:00:42.851 --> 00:00:44.075
- Well, I'd say get in the ring

00:00:44.075 --> 00:00:45.483
and have a go and see what it's like.

00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:47.302
And see the hard work, dedication,

00:00:47.302 --> 00:00:48.635
the athleticism some people have.

00:00:48.635 --> 00:00:49.635
(groaning)

00:00:49.635 --> 00:00:51.730
Someone goes down and it
looks like a nasty fall

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:52.983
and you have no idea whether they're

00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:54.596
actually legitimately hurt or not.

00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:56.054
(groaning)

00:00:56.054 --> 00:00:57.263
Even though you're
sitting there and you know

00:00:57.263 --> 00:00:59.112
that you're watching
a bit of a soap opera,

00:00:59.112 --> 00:01:00.855
you've got this mystery about it.

00:01:00.855 --> 00:01:02.651
- You never know what part
is real and what's fake?

00:01:02.651 --> 00:01:03.626
- Yeah.

00:01:03.626 --> 00:01:06.376
(dramatic music)

00:01:07.353 --> 00:01:12.156
- [Narrator] Wilbur Force,
you will teach me your art.

00:01:12.156 --> 00:01:14.739
Dare I remember your best self.

00:01:17.105 --> 00:01:21.151
- What if my wrestling character
embodied your weaknesses?

00:01:21.151 --> 00:01:22.166
Like laziness.

00:01:22.166 --> 00:01:23.904
I could wear your mask.

00:01:23.904 --> 00:01:25.459
- I don't want it to be public knowledge

00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:26.808
that I've got sleep apnea.

00:01:26.808 --> 00:01:29.365
It's not something that I
want to wave the flag of.

00:01:29.365 --> 00:01:32.039
Hey, I'm a failure, wicked, awesome!

00:01:32.039 --> 00:01:33.597
- That's how I pitched the film, though.

00:01:33.597 --> 00:01:37.110
- "Wilbur, can we make our film
please, about 'ze wrestling?"

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.802
I'm like, alright, sure.

00:01:38.802 --> 00:01:42.487
Next minute, "Wilbur,
why are you so fat, yah?"

00:01:42.487 --> 00:01:44.353
"Why are you so fatty-fatty?"

00:01:44.353 --> 00:01:46.490
- It's like you just
want to show me around.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:49.082
This is my friend, he does nothing.

00:01:49.082 --> 00:01:50.524
Come and laugh at him.
- No, it's about.

00:01:50.524 --> 00:01:51.607
- That's what you're
trying to do, isn't it?

00:01:51.607 --> 00:01:53.137
- It's about you and me and me setting out

00:01:53.137 --> 00:01:55.719
to make this film and
get you off your ass.

00:01:55.719 --> 00:01:57.375
- [Wilbur] So I'm a little
tool so you can create drama.

00:01:57.375 --> 00:01:59.584
You're just using it, you're
not being a friend at all.

00:01:59.584 --> 00:02:01.066
I don't wanna do this anymore.

00:02:01.066 --> 00:02:02.650
- You're mic-ed up.
- Take this shit off.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.298
Pull over!

00:02:04.298 --> 00:02:07.323
- Will.
- (beep) off.

00:02:07.323 --> 00:02:08.493
(car door slams)

00:02:08.493 --> 00:02:10.609
- For (beep) sakes.

00:02:10.609 --> 00:02:11.627
(car door slams)

00:02:11.627 --> 00:02:12.651
- Will!

00:02:12.651 --> 00:02:15.953
- [Wilbur] (beep) off.

00:02:15.953 --> 00:02:17.536
(beeping)

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:20.953
(scuffling and grunting)

00:02:21.919 --> 00:02:24.502
(car whoosing)

00:02:28.236 --> 00:02:31.041
- [Narrator] Wilbur Force,
Wilbur Force, Wilbur Force.

00:02:31.041 --> 00:02:33.464
Wilbur Force, Wilbur Force.

00:02:33.464 --> 00:02:36.214
(dramatic music)

00:02:54.003 --> 00:02:57.438
(muffled shouting)

00:02:57.438 --> 00:03:00.188
(dramatic music)

